 | `GGML_VK_CONCAT_TRANSPOSE` | **ON when unset.** Only an exact `0` disables. Added 2026-09-04. | Scope: `GGML_OP_CONCAT` where `src1` is transposed (`nb[0] > nb[1]`) and `src0` has `ne[2] == ne[3] == 1` — the delta-net conv-state shape, and nothing else. That shape sends the generic concat down a 40960-byte stride (`conv_channels * 4`), one cache line per element and one memory channel per row; the gate routes it to a 32×32 tiled kernel with a `[32][33]` padded shared tile so the strided read coalesces and the write stays linear. The predicate falls back to the generic concat when the tiled grid would exceed `maxComputeWorkGroupCount`. Disjoint from the pre-existing `cpy_transpose_02_32/02_16` tiled branch. | Leave it on. Set `0` to reproduce the BEFORE arm, or if a device's tiled dispatch misbehaves. | **Op-level WIN, serve-level TIE, both measured; the tie is not a loss.** RIG-A, one binary with the arms env-gated, Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B-abliterated-UD Q4_K_XL on the seat serve line, 4 interleaved launches / 32 graph blocks, Balanced: CONCAT **2550.2 → 2224.1 µs per dispatch = −12.79%**, **−15.66 ms per `ub512` prefill graph**, arms **non-overlapping** (`min(OFF) 2510.5 > max(ON) 2325.7`). On a default-branch binary ten commits later, a position-1-excluded median over three takes (9 launches): **−11.4349% / −13.988 ms**. Both banked; neither replaces the other (different binaries, and per the equipment register a possibly different memory configuration).<br>**The end-to-end claim is a TIE and must stay one.** CONCAT is **1.42%** of the prefill graph here, so the ceiling is **+0.18%** — far under this box's paired CI95 halfwidths of **±6.7% / ±5.9% / ±31.2%**. Two counterbalanced 8-launch palindromes both read TIED at `pp512@ub512`, `pp2048@ub512`, `pp2048@ub2048`, with the **sign flipping between takes on two of three shapes**; neither direction is quotable. Upstream's **+3.3% pp2048** was measured on gfx1151 where the op is a larger share — **upstream-reported, not reproduced, not contradicted.**<br>**Quality:** generated text **byte-identical ON vs OFF, 3/3 prompts**, temp 0, on two genuinely separate processes (distinct ports, each listener proven a descendant of its own launcher — an earlier ON-vs-ON result on a shared port was **VOID and is withdrawn**); F-141 content floor **0/8 on every slot**; reachability **1392 generation-time dispatches ON vs 0 OFF**. `test-backend-ops -o CONCAT` **195/195, 0 FAIL, both arms** — but that suite provably carries **no transposed-`src1` case**, so it proves non-regression, **not coverage**. **UNMEASURED:** the decode/verify graph, and MoE models (where the upstream claims live). |
 | `GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES` | **ON when unset — this row inverts the usual shape of this registry, read it before assuming.** Specialization constant 3; default `1` = read scales directly from the block. **`GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES=0` restores upstream's shared-memory staging path byte for byte.** One binary serves both arms; the host prints the resolved mode on stderr at pipeline creation. Added 2026-09-05. | Scope: `mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp` only. Upstream stages all 16 int8 scales of the superblock into a double-buffered shared tile and pays a `barrier()` **per row, inside the row loop** — the only `q*_k` mat-vec that does; `q4_k` and `q5_k` unpack in registers with no barrier. The exchange moves no data between threads: the 16 threads share one block, each writes its own scale and each reads only four bytes of that same block, off the cache line the staging already fetched. Direct reads yield identical values in identical fma order, so the result is **bit-identical by construction** and measured so. | **Leave it at the default and do not quote it as a speed lever.** Set `0` to A/B the two paths on other hardware, or to fall back if a driver mishandles the specialization constant. It is a plausible win where barriers are costlier or shared memory is scarcer than on gfx1103 — **unmeasured there**. | **MEASURED NEUTRAL on RIG-A. No speed win is claimed and none may be quoted.** Seat line (Huihui UD-Q4_K_XL + DFlash2 Q4_K_M drafter at `--spec-draft-n-max 2`, so verify width 3), one binary, arms env-gated, **6 position-balanced interleaved launches per phase**, Balanced power plan, 32+16 GB asymmetric RAM: op level, `q6_k` rows read a median ON/OFF ratio **0.9796** against **its own control of 78 untouched op rows at median 1.0061, p10–p90 [0.9479, 1.0636]** (one binary, env-gated); the two-binary diagnostic read **0.9880** against **0.9990, p10–p90 [0.9520, 1.0527]** — **no `q6_k` row separates from the control band in either pairing.** Serve level **TIED on all six cells** — prefill and decode reported separately at three prompt lengths, every arm range overlapping. Identity: **byte-identical output, one distinct sha256 per prompt across 6 serve launches (18 completions)**. Correctness `test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT` **1394/1394, 0 FAIL, both arms**.<br>**Kept on the distributable-engine ground, not on a measured gain:** strictly less work — one fewer workgroup barrier per row per superblock and no shared tile — for a bit-identical result.<br>**What it did NOT fix, stated:** `q6_K` mat-vec runs **~35% below `q5_K`** at the identical shape (`m=17408 n=3 k=5120`: **41.0 vs 63.8 GB/s**, ratio 0.643), every `q6_K` row in a 39.2–41.6 band. The per-row barrier was the leading mechanism for that deficit and is now **FALSIFIED**; the deficit is **OPEN**. Correction to the motivating claim: `q4_K` at that same shape is **60.6 GB/s, not 72.5** — the deficit survives on the `q5_K` comparison only. See [`FINDINGS.md`](FINDINGS.md) F-14. |
 | ROCmFP4-FAST `q8_1` MMVQ width gate | **Code, not an environment variable. No new environment variable was added for this mechanism** — the pre-existing `GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ=1` is the only runtime lever, and it is upstream's, applying to every MMVQ type rather than this one (its own measured effect on `Q2_0_G128` is in the `GGML_ARIFI_G128_MMV_ROWS` row above). `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq` returns true for `GGML_TYPE_Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST` on AMD at **`n == 3` and `n == 5` only**; every other width takes the f32 dequant shader. | Scope: the `q8_1` integer-dot mat-vec and mat-vec-id pipelines for `Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST`. Before the port the selector **listed** the type and `should_use_mmvq` **returned true**, but no line ever created the pipeline — so activations were quantized on every mat-vec, the lookup returned null, and the backend fell back to f32 in silence, paying the quantize cost for nothing. The port creates the pipelines and adds the repack and dot product (ue4m3 scale, exact-int LUT so `d_a * d_b * int-dot` forms the same product the f32 path does). | **Do not enable it more widely, and do not put this on a default branch yet.** Width 3 is the verify width of a depth-2 draft, which is where the gain is. Width 1 is a measured tie; width 4 is a tie; width 2 is the width that changed a sampled token; above 5 the port loses. | **MEASURED WIN, INTEGRATION BLOCKED.** Ladder, RIG-A, `m=17408 k=5120`, 3-round medians, epoch E2: `n=1` ×0.991, `n=2` ×1.192, **`n=3` ×1.361**, `n=4` ×1.018, **`n=5` ×1.310**, `n=8` ×1.025. Epoch E1 read ×0.998 / ×1.183 / ×1.335 / ×1.015 / ×1.316 / ×1.040 — **the gains reproduce across a driver change**. The discriminator is the control arm: under `GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ=1` both arms take the identical f32 shader and every row flattens to **×0.991–1.007**, so this is the port and not build drift. Ungated at `n=8` the port read **×0.796**, which is why the gate has an upper bound at all.<br>**Serve, epoch E2** (julianmb Qwen3.8-27B-ROCmFP4-FAST 14.56 GB, DFlash2 depth 2, palindrome, 16 rounds/slot): drafted decode **7.498 → 9.518 t/s mean, +2.0199 [1.3212, 2.7186], 8/8 cells positive = +27%**; median 7.461 → 9.282. Plain **5.084 → 5.086, +0.0016 [−0.0168, +0.0199] = tied**. Prefill tied. Rolled **32/40 → 33/40**. **Zero empty completions in 64 rounds.** F-141 **0/8** on all three slots; `test-backend-ops` **10 MUL_MAT + 2 MUL_MAT_ID cases, 0 FAIL**.<br>**BLOCKING RESIDUAL, and it is why widths 2 and 4 are excluded:** an earlier build of this port made the model emit an empty completion — first token end-of-generation — deterministically on one prompt on this file. Three hypotheses were falsified before the cause was isolated to **width 2** (the n=1 dispatch gate did not remove it; a slot-swap proved the empties follow the **binary**, not the slot; forcing f32 for the whole run removed them). The same shader arithmetic is **still live at widths 3 and 5**, and the reproducer is a plain sequence that cannot reach them. Owed before default-branch integration: an adversarial drafted-mode cache-history corpus reaching width 3, or an MMVQ-vs-f32 logits comparison, or a tightened backend error gate. See [`FINDINGS.md`](FINDINGS.md) F-13. |
-| `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` | **OFF when unset.** Only an exact `1` admits `GGML_TYPE_SX8` in `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()`; unset and every other value leave every width on the f32 dequant mat-vec. Added 2026-09-10 (lane-230/R46 commit C). | Scope: the `q8_1` integer-dot `mul_mat_vec` pipeline for `GGML_TYPE_SX8` and nothing else. The pipeline is created unconditionally beside the `Q8_0` row and the `b_type == Q8_1` selector switch lists the type; this env var is the only thing that makes `quantize_y` true, so with it unset the pipeline is compiled and never dispatched. The `_id` mirror is deliberately NOT admitted (declared with an `ARIFI-SYNC-SET ... EXCEPT SX8=` marker): no id `q8_1` pipeline is generated for S-X8, so admitting it there would select a null pipeline. | **Only on the 248320x5120 embed/output shape, and only while investigating.** That is where B2's `n <= 3` whole-block gate hands wide batches back to the per-position kernel and this path is worth +38 to +97%. Do not enable it for a general serve: the FFN shapes lose. | **MEASURED, MIXED, so it ships OFF.** RIG-A, `test-backend-ops`, 3 interleaved rounds per arm in one quiet hold, base = the unchanged kernel, candidate = commit C on top of the gated commit B2 (`32-paired-c.txt`, 96 cells, raw timings in `32-paired-c.json`). **Against the SHIPPED kernel it loses at `n=7` on three of four primary 27B shapes** - `-28.37%` (4096x14336), `-26.13%` (17408x5120), `-13.29%` (5120x17408) - **raw rounds non-overlapping**, so repeatable, not noise. The PREREG promotion bar (>5% median at `n=1..4`, no >3% repeatable regression on any primary shape) is also missed at `n=4`, 4096x14336: `-6.85%` against B2 (DERIVED, cross-session). **Where it wins it wins large**: 248320x5120 `+38.00 / +45.73 / +46.43 / +51.79%` at `n=1..4` against the unchanged kernel, `+94.85%` at `n=6`. A per-width admit was REFUSED as overfitting - the winning region is one shape at two widths. The `n=7` cliff is **non-monotonic** (`+13.69 / -13.88 / +17.68%` at `n=6/7/8` on 5120x17408 against B2), which points at a `NUM_COLS == 7` tail defect in the mmvq framework rather than a tuning loss; that is where a narrowed admit must start. Routing was proven by a **planted-RED in commit C's dot product only**: with the env unset every `sx8` MUL_MAT case is green, with `=1` ten of twelve go red and the two `mul_mm` cases stay green. Evidence: `research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-10-lane-230-r46-sx8-mmv/`. |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` | **THIS ROW INVERTED on 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b phase 2) - read it before assuming the old default.** **ON when unset, wherever the MMVQ A-side hoist is live** (device-probed ON for AMD): `GGML_TYPE_SX8` takes the `q8_1` integer-dot mat-vec at EVERY width, and only an exact `0` hands it back to the whole-block f32 route. Where the hoist is off (`GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0`, non-AMD) or the routing is pinned back (`GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE=legacy`), the pre-R48b rule below still holds: **OFF when unset, only an exact `1` admits the type**. The character test is unchanged in both directions (`env[0]`, not `atoi()` - they disagree on `"2"` and `"01"`). | Scope: the `q8_1` integer-dot `mul_mat_vec` pipeline for `GGML_TYPE_SX8` and nothing else, on the plain `MUL_MAT` path. The `_id` path calls the same predicate and so now admits the type as well, but `ggml_vk_get_dequantize_mul_mat_vec_id()` still returns `nullptr` for S-X8 at `b_type == Q8_1` and the caller's `if (dmmv == nullptr)` branch (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:13246-13250`) clears `quantize_y` and reselects the f16 dequant pipeline - CHECKED, not assumed: `MUL_MAT_ID -b Vulkan0` is a receipt of this commit. | **Default. Enable the `0` arm only to pair against the whole-block route, or on a device where the hoist is off.** | **The pre-R48b evidence for the OFF default, and what superseded it.** The n=7 cliff that kept this OFF was an A-side re-decode in the mat-vec nest, and lane-235/R48b removed it. Under forced MMVQ with the hoist ON, S-X8 is FLAT at the bus at `n=1..8` (248320x5120: `74.8/75.2/72.1/73.6/74.2/74.7/73.7/72.8` GB/s; FFN shapes 36-37 at every width) against `62/70/33.5/45.5` at `n=5..8` with the hoist OFF, and beats the SHIPPED whole-block route by **+40..+110% at n>=4** on 248320x5120 and **+15 / +34% at n=2/3** on 17408x5120 (`32-paired-r48bforce.txt` vs `32-paired-r46iq.txt`, HQ, 3 quiet interleaved rounds, same binary both arms). **Still owed: a DEFAULT-routing re-pair** - every number here is from a `GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ=1` arm. The original evidence, unchanged and still the reason the `0` path exists (added 2026-09-10, lane-230/R46 commit C): **MEASURED, MIXED, which is why it shipped OFF then.** RIG-A, `test-backend-ops`, 3 interleaved rounds per arm in one quiet hold, base = the unchanged kernel, candidate = commit C on top of the gated commit B2 (`32-paired-c.txt`, 96 cells, raw timings in `32-paired-c.json`). **Against the SHIPPED kernel it loses at `n=7` on three of four primary 27B shapes** - `-28.37%` (4096x14336), `-26.13%` (17408x5120), `-13.29%` (5120x17408) - **raw rounds non-overlapping**, so repeatable, not noise. The PREREG promotion bar (>5% median at `n=1..4`, no >3% repeatable regression on any primary shape) is also missed at `n=4`, 4096x14336: `-6.85%` against B2 (DERIVED, cross-session). **Where it wins it wins large**: 248320x5120 `+38.00 / +45.73 / +46.43 / +51.79%` at `n=1..4` against the unchanged kernel, `+94.85%` at `n=6`. A per-width admit was REFUSED as overfitting - the winning region is one shape at two widths. The `n=7` cliff is **non-monotonic** (`+13.69 / -13.88 / +17.68%` at `n=6/7/8` on 5120x17408 against B2), which points at a `NUM_COLS == 7` tail defect in the mmvq framework rather than a tuning loss; that is where a narrowed admit must start. Routing was proven by a **planted-RED in commit C's dot product only**: with the env unset every `sx8` MUL_MAT case is green, with `=1` ten of twelve go red and the two `mul_mm` cases stay green. Evidence: `research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-10-lane-230-r46-sx8-mmv/`. |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST` | **ON by device probe when unset on AMD, OFF on every other vendor** — the only vendor this was measured on. Specialization constant 3 of `mul_mat_vecq.comp`; `1` = decode each row's weight block once per (row, k-slice) into registers and loop the columns doing only the B load and the integer dot, `0` = the inherited nest, which re-runs the whole A decode once per column. Only an exact `0` or `1` is taken; anything else falls back to the probe. Added 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b). | Scope: every `q8_1` integer-dot `mul_mat_vec` pipeline. Both nests call the same `mmvq_load_a()` / `mmvq_dot_a()` pair in the same order, so results are **bit-identical by construction** and this is a scheduling change only. `NUM_COLS == 1` folds to the inherited nest at pipeline-compile time. Probed once at device creation, because routing reads the same answer. Two narrowings ride on top: `IQ1_S`/`IQ1_M` are OFF by default on register grounds (see the next row) and the legacy-block family (`Q4_0`, `Q4_1`, `Q5_0`, `Q5_1`, `Q8_0`, `MXFP4`) is OFF at `NUM_COLS >= 6`. **`=0` is the widest switch in this group: it removes the hoisted nest AND the R48b routing that depends on it.** | Default. Use `=0` for the OFF arm of a pairing — one binary serves both arms — or on a vendor this has not been measured on. | **Correctness CLEARED, default-route performance UNMEASURED.** `test-backend-ops MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0` is 0 FAIL in both arms, and two planted reds proved the decode site live (RED-1, fires in both arms) and the hoisted nest the one serving (RED-2, red ON / green OFF). HQ forced-MMVQ pairing (`32-paired-r48bforce.txt`, 3 quiet interleaved rounds, same binary): the hoist removes a **10-15x tail cliff** at `NUM_COLS` 6..7 for `q4_K` (248320x5120 `5.1 / 3.3` → `52 / 48` GB/s; 5120x17408 `3.7 / 2.5` → `26.8 / 24.3`) and holds S-X8 flat at the bus across `n=1..8`. It **REGRESSES Q8_0 at `n>=6`** (`-25 / -17 / -24%` at `n=6/7/8` on 4096x14336, `-17%` at `n=8` on 5120x17408, `-10%` at `n=6` on 248320x5120), which is what the legacy-family `NUM_COLS >= 6` gate is for. `q5_K` at `n=1`, its only MMVQ width, is a wash. Every number here is from a `GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ=1` arm; a **default-routing re-pair is owed**. |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST_IQ1` | **OFF when unset.** Only an exact `1` turns the A-side hoist on for the `IQ1_S` and `IQ1_M` `q8_1` pipelines, and never above the global switch — `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` forces it off regardless. Added 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b). | Scope: the `IQ1_S` and `IQ1_M` `q8_1` `mul_mat_vec` pipelines only. They carry the largest A state of any MMVQ type (10 and 12 registers per row against 5-6 for the K-quants) and run the most rows per workgroup (`rm_iq_int` = 4 or 8), the highest product in the register table. Gated in the HOST, not by an `#ifdef`: the shader keeps both paths, so no rebuild moves it. | Only to pair the IQ1 types specifically. | **UNMEASURED on these two types — that is exactly why they ship OFF.** The default is a register-pressure judgement (report section 3 of `OPUS-R48B-MMVQ-A-HOIST-REPORT.md`), not a measurement. Arithmetic is identical either way; correctness is covered by the same `MUL_MAT` sweep. |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_ROUTE` | **unset = R48b routing.** Only the exact string `legacy` pins `ggml_vk_should_use_mmvq()` back to the pre-R48b rules while KEEPING the hoisted nest. Added 2026-09-14 (lane-235/R48b phase 2). | Scope: two AMD routing rules, and nothing else. (i) `GGML_TYPE_SX8` → MMVQ at every width (`legacy`: opt-in via `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=1`). (ii) `GGML_TYPE_Q4_K` at `n >= 5` → MMVQ when `k <= 8192`, f32 above (`legacy`: f32 at every `n >= 5`). `Q5_K`, `Q8_0` and the legacy-block family are untouched in both modes. Both rules are additionally gated on the hoist being live, so on a non-AMD device or under `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0` they are already the legacy rules. **`legacy` is NOT the same arm as `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0`**: this one keeps the hoisted nest and changes only where traffic is sent, the other removes the nest as well. A pairing log must say which was used. | Use `legacy` to pair the ROUTING change alone, holding the kernel constant. | **Routing derived from the HQ forced-MMVQ pairing, not yet re-measured at default routing.** `q4_K` MMVQ+hoist vs the f32 default at `n=5..8`: 248320x5120 (k=5120) `55.7/52.1/48.0/45.6` vs `46.0/36.1/35.0/29.0` GB/s (**+21/+44/+37/+57%**), 17408x5120 (k=5120) `35.7/34.8/33.5/31.3` vs `33.2/27.9/29.9/24.4` (win), 5120x17408 (**k=17408**) `32.4/26.8/24.3/22.7` vs `37.0/30.8/31.6/27.2` (**LOSS**) — hence the `k` split. `k = 8192` is the midpoint of the two measured `k` values and is an **untested boundary**: nothing was run between 5120 and 17408. S-X8 evidence is in the `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` row above. |
